# the wasm object as a neutral object and back
#
# a wasm object's index spaces become entries: its types first, then its
# imports in the order the import section lists them, each in its kind's space,
# then the definitions of each space, functions, tables, memories, globals and
# tags, then its data segments. the entry order states the import order across
# the spaces, and the module built back lists its imports in entry order. a function's entry names its type entry as
# its signature, an import's entry its module and field, and a defined
# function's or segment's entry its section. every defined function is one text
# section of its body, every data segment one section named, aligned and
# flagged as its segment info states and of the kind its name spells, a
# zero-fill kind's bytes zero fill, and every custom section the conventions do
# not consume one debug or metadata section. the symbol table's entries are the
# object's symbols in order, a function, global, table or tag symbol defined at
# its entry, a data symbol placed in its segment's section, and a section
# symbol at its section. the relocation records of each reloc section are
# relocations of the function, segment or custom section they fall in, each of
# the kind its type maps to. COMDATs are groups, init functions give their
# function sections a priority, and an exported symbol an export directive.
# what the neutral model has no record for travels in facts keyed by the
# format: each type, each table, memory, global and tag type, each segment's
# head, each element segment, the data count, the start function, the exports
# and the producers, so the module built back holds what the file held. the
# target features are the object's wasm-features trait, which a link merges,
# and every import names the undefined symbol the link resolves it by, one the
# symbol table names none for a symbol of its field. a core section, a custom
# section a convention consumes or a linking subsection the reader held raw is
# refused, naming it, as the facts it holds would be lost.
#
# a module without a linking section converts as a module: it states no
# symbol, and its data segments, which no segment info names, are unnamed
# data sections of no alignment. its name section is a metadata section of
# its payload, as for an object. a module of a kind a link takes as an object
# is built with its linking and reloc sections, and any other with neither,
# refusing an object that holds what only they carry.
#
# an object's records are lowered into a copy of it, its line records as a
# DWARF line table in the .debug_line custom section. a label the lowering
# places in a function body has no wasm symbol, as a function symbol names
# its function whole, and a relocation from one is written as the function
# offset of its width from a local function symbol of the body, its addend
# the label's offset in the body, as the tool conventions' DWARF document
# gives code addresses as offsets in the code section.
#
# the module built from an object lays the sections out in the order the
# specification fixes, then the custom sections in object order, then the
# linking section, the reloc sections and the producers and target features.
# in an object a section size and a linking subsection size are padded to five
# bytes, as clang pads them, and in a module a section size takes its shortest
# form, as every other number does.

